1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,667
Bitter cold, almost dark: the last evening
of the year.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:09,917
A poor girl shuffled along in her mother's
big slippers.

3
00:00:10,508 --> 00:00:14,875
Carriages raced by; she lost them, and
went on barefoot.

4
00:00:15,467 --> 00:00:17,750
Matches… who'll buy my matches?

5
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:21,167
No one had bought a single match.

6
00:00:21,758 --> 00:00:26,125
Candles gleamed in the windows; it smelled
of roast goose.

7
00:00:26,883 --> 00:00:32,083
She huddled in a corner, afraid to go home
to her father.

8
00:00:32,717 --> 00:00:37,083
Her hands were numb. If she dared strike
just one…

9
00:00:38,675 --> 00:00:43,875
How it blazed! A warm iron stove seemed to
stand before her.

10
00:00:44,175 --> 00:00:46,042
Then it went out.

11
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:52,417
A second: the wall became a veil, and
inside, a roast goose steamed.

12
00:00:53,008 --> 00:00:56,958
It hopped down and waddled toward her —
then darkness.

13
00:00:57,758 --> 00:01:02,542
A third: she sat beneath a Christmas tree
ablaze with candles.

14
00:01:03,217 --> 00:01:08,000
Out it went. The lights rose and became
stars. One fell.

15
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,750
Someone is dying.

16
00:01:10,467 --> 00:01:14,733
Her grandmother, the only one who had
loved her,

17
00:01:14,733 --> 00:01:19,000
had said: a falling star is a soul going
to God.

18
00:01:19,592 --> 00:01:23,542
A fourth — and there stood Grandmother,
shining and kind.

19
00:01:24,217 --> 00:01:26,500
Grandmother! Take me with you!

20
00:01:27,258 --> 00:01:31,208
She struck the whole bundle, to keep her
near.

21
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:36,287
Grandmother took her in her arms, and they
flew up,

22
00:01:36,287 --> 00:01:40,000
where there is no cold, no hunger, no
fear.

23
00:01:40,592 --> 00:01:46,208
At dawn she sat there still, rosy-cheeked
and smiling — frozen to death.

24
00:01:46,925 --> 00:01:49,208
She wanted to warm herself.

25
00:01:49,842 --> 00:01:56,708
No one knew the beautiful things she had
seen, or the joy she had gone to.

